>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div>
        <header class="page-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">A PERSON BEHIND THE IDEAS</p><h1>
            Hi, I’m Guoran.<br />Call me <em>Future.</em>
          </h1><p>
            I read too many of Asimov’s robot stories as a kid. They sent me
            toward AI—and toward bigger questions about what intelligence means
            for the world we’re building.
          </p>
        </header><a class="text-link" href="mailto:i2754067952@gmail.com"
          >Say hello <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div><figure>
        <img
          class="about-portrait"
          src="/assets/images/pfp.jpg"
          alt="Guoran Hu"
          width="360"
          height="450"
        /><figcaption class="portrait-caption">
          <span>GUORAN “FUTURE” HU</span><span>ABU DHABI, UAE</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>
        <span class="eyebrow">THE WAY I LOOK AT THINGS</span>Across the
        boundaries.
      </h2><div class="about-body">
        <p>
          I’m drawn to the connections between AI, philosophy, economics, and
          complex systems. Each gives me a different way to look at the same
          world. None feels sufficient on its own.
        </p><p>
          My research interests center on world models: how machines can
          represent their surroundings, simulate what might happen, and learn to
          act. I’m interested in generative models, reinforcement learning,
          robotics, and the safety questions that come with more capable agents.
        </p><p>
          Outside research, I enjoy tinkering with small side projects for fun,
          following an idea and seeing where it leads.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="now" class="about-section">
      <h2>
        <span class="eyebrow">CURRENTLY & ALONG THE WAY</span>Learning by doing.
      </h2><div>
        <ExperienceTimeline />
